#Install Hyperledger Iroha on Ubuntu VM using Docker and perform transactions and queries.

Super Short Flow
Install VM → Install Ubuntu → Install Docker → Create Volume → Clone Iroha → Run Iroha → Open CLI → Create Domain → Create Asset → Add Quantity → Query Asset
PART A – Create Ubuntu VM
Step 1: Install Requirements
Install VMware Player/Workstation
Download Ubuntu ISO

Step 2: Create Virtual Machine

In VMware:

File → New Virtual Machine
Choose:
Typical

Step 3: Select Ubuntu ISO
Choose:
Installer disc image file (iso)
Browse Ubuntu ISO
Click Next

Step 4: Configure VM

Set:

Disk Size = 25 GB
RAM = 4 GB
Store as single file

Then click Finish.

Step 5: Install Ubuntu
Start VM
Follow Ubuntu installation steps

Ubuntu gets installed inside VMware.

PART B – Install Docker
Step 6: Open Ubuntu Terminal

Run:

sudo apt-get install curl
Step 7: Install Docker

Run:

curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo apt-key add -
sudo add-apt-repository "deb [arch=amd64] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu $(lsb_release -cs) stable"
sudo apt-get update
apt-cache policy docker-ce
sudo apt-get install -y docker-ce

PART C – Setup Hyperledger Iroha
Step 8: Create Docker Volume
sudo docker volume create blockstore

Purpose:

Stores blockchain data permanently

Step 9: Install Git & Clone Iroha
sudo apt-get install git
git clone -b develop https://github.com/hyperledger/iroha --depth=1

Step 10: Run Iroha Docker Container
sudo docker run -it --name iroha \
-p 50051:50051 \
-v $(pwd)/iroha/example:/opt/iroha_data \
-v blockstore:/tmp/block_store \
--network=srcmake-iroha-network \
--entrypoint=/bin/bash \
hyperledger/iroha:x86_64-develop-latest

Step 11: Start Iroha
irohad --config config.docker --genesis_block genesis.block --keypair_name node0

Purpose:

Starts blockchain node

Step 12: Open Another Terminal & Attach Container
sudo docker exec -it iroha /bin/bash

Step 13: Open Iroha CLI
iroha-cli --account_name admin@test
